        {
          // the sheet only marks the chosen weapon kinds; the mastery properties aren't calculated
          "key": "barbarian.weapon-mastery",
          "name": "Weapon Mastery",
          "level": 1,
          "description": "<p>Your training with weapons allows you to use the mastery properties of two kinds of Simple or Martial Melee weapons of your choice, such as <em>Greataxes</em> and <em>Handaxes</em>. Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can practice weapon drills and change one of those weapon choices.</p><p>When you reach certain Barbarian levels, you gain the ability to use the mastery properties of more kinds of weapons, as shown in the Weapon Mastery column of the Barbarian Features table.</p><h5>Using Weapon Mastery</h5><p>Each kind of weapon has one mastery property. While you attack with a weapon of a chosen kind, you can use its property; the sheet marks the chosen weapons but doesn't apply the property for you. Only Melee weapons count for the Barbarian.</p><ul><li><strong>Cleave.</strong> After a melee hit, make one more attack against a second creature within 5 feet of the first (no ability modifier to its damage unless negative); once per turn.</li><li><strong>Graze.</strong> On a miss, deal damage equal to the ability modifier of the attack.</li><li><strong>Nick.</strong> Make the extra attack of the Light property as part of the Attack action; once per turn.</li><li><strong>Push.</strong> On a hit, push a Large or smaller creature up to 10 feet away.</li><li><strong>Sap.</strong> On a hit, the creature has Disadvantage on its next attack roll before your next turn.</li><li><strong>Slow.</strong> On a hit that deals damage, reduce the creature's Speed by 10 feet until your next turn.</li><li><strong>Topple.</strong> On a hit, the creature makes a Constitution save (DC 8 + the attack's ability modifier + your Proficiency Bonus) or has the Prone condition.</li><li><strong>Vex.</strong> On a hit that deals damage, you have Advantage on your next attack roll against that creature before the end of your next turn.</li></ul>",
          "choices": [
